# Hermes Wildfire IM Platform Adapter

A [Hermes Agent](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent) platform plugin that bridges Hermes with [Wildfire IM](https://www.wildfirechat.cn/) through the [robot-gateway](https://github.com/wildfirechat/robot-gateway) WebSocket protocol.

## Features

- **Bidirectional messaging**: receive messages from Wildfire IM users/groups and send Hermes replies back.
- **Auto reconnect**: exponential-backoff reconnect to `robot-gateway`.
- **Group filtering**: only reply in groups when @mentioned, the message ends with `?`, or it contains help keywords (configurable).
- **Media support**: text, image, file, and video messages (files are uploaded via `robot-gateway` first).
- **Session isolation**: one Hermes session per user DM and per group.

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────┐     WebSocket      ┌──────────────┐     HTTP/RobotService     ┌──────────┐
│  Hermes     │ ◀──robot-gateway──▶ │ robot-gateway │ ◀──────────────────────▶ │ Wildfire │
│  Agent      │    protocol        │ (ws :8884)    │                         │   IM     │
└─────────────┘                    └──────────────┘                         └──────────┘
```

## Installation

### Option 1: Directory plugin (recommended for development)

```bash
# Clone or copy this repo into the Hermes plugins directory
git clone https://github.com/your-org/hermes-wildfire.git ~/.hermes/plugins/hermes-wildfire

# Restart Hermes gateway
hermes gateway restart
```

### Option 2: pip package

```bash
pip install -e .
# Hermes will discover the plugin via the `hermes_agent.plugins` entry point.
hermes gateway restart
```

## Configuration

### Environment variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `WILDFIRE_GATEWAY_URL` | Yes | `ws://host:8884/robot/gateway` |
| `WILDFIRE_ROBOT_ID` | Yes | Wildfire IM robot ID |
| `WILDFIRE_ROBOT_SECRET` | Yes | Wildfire IM robot secret |
| `WILDFIRE_HOME_CHANNEL` | No | Default `user:userId` or `group:groupId` for cron/notifications |
| `WILDFIRE_REQUIRE_MENTION` | No | `true` to require @mention/help keywords in groups (default `true`) |
| `WILDFIRE_HELP_KEYWORDS` | No | Comma-separated keywords, e.g. `帮,请,分析,总结` |
| `WILDFIRE_ALLOWED_USERS` | No | Comma-separated user IDs allowed to DM the bot |
| `WILDFIRE_ALLOWED_GROUPS` | No | Comma-separated group IDs the bot may join |

### `config.yaml`

```yaml
wildfire:
  enabled: true
  gateway_url: ws://localhost:8884/robot/gateway
  robot_id: YourRobotId
  robot_secret: YourRobotSecret
  require_mention: true
  help_keywords: "帮,请,分析,总结,怎么,如何"
```

## Usage

After the gateway is running:

```bash
hermes gateway status
```

You should see **Wildfire IM** listed as a connected platform.

In Wildfire IM, search for your robot ID and start a chat:

- **Private chat**: every message is forwarded to Hermes.
- **Group chat**: the bot only responds when:
  - It is @mentioned, **or**
  - The message ends with `?` / `？`, **or**
  - The message contains one of the configured help keywords.

## Development

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
```

